{{also|Klick}}
==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[click]]

===Etymology===
* Most likely a pseudo-condensed pronunciation of {{term|kilometre}}.
* Possibly onomatopoeic of the sound of a military odometer.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{slang|military}} A [[kilometre]].
#: The term is used in countries that have adopted the metric system. In the USA, it is commonly used in war and science fiction films; for example, ''the target is 5 '''klicks''' north''.

====Quotations====
* '''2002''', [[w:Robert J. Sawyer|Robert J. Sawyer]], "Hominids":
*: an asteroid between one and three kilometers wide had slammed into the ground at fifteen '''klicks''' per second.

